  "description": "Fuselage: White upper and forward fuselage; a large red five-pointed star behind the forward door at window level; a huge brown California grizzly bear walking aft over the window line from about the forward cabin to the wing, standing on a green grass strip; lower aft fuselage and belly red (the flag's red bar) from the wing to the tail. Cheatlines: None. Tail: Heart fin (blue/red/yellow) with white 'Southwest'. Engines: Green cowlings with brown bear-fur artwork continuing over them. Winglets: approximate: white. Titles: 'Southwest' white on lower fin; 'California One' small by cockpit. Artwork: California 'Bear Flag'. Colors hex: approximate.",
