  "notes": "Drawn from July 2026 photos of N8653A (both sides; the design is mirrored, so the bear walks forward on each). The bear is drawn as one silhouette; its maroon shading is described. Belly between the engines not seen squarely. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the fin is the state jets' Heart fin as re-measured on Colorado One, copied with its title and flag. 'California One' measured on the July 2026 right-side photo against the nose and the forward door (2.2-3.5 m back), two weights, a pair of titles per side (the left side mirrored, reading nose to tail), on Colorado One's line under the cockpit windows. The red bar's and the grass band's curved edges made smooth.",
  "history": "Previously on N609SW and N943WN."
